# Kit stack detection

Never assume the stack or the test runner.

1. Run `./scripts/kit detect-stack --write-profile` from the kit, or read the cached
   `.claude/stack.profile.json` in the current project when it is already present.
2. Take `test`, `lint`, `typecheck`, and `security` commands from that profile —
   not from memory.
3. `skills_to_load` in the profile lists the pattern skills that apply.

User stack-specific rules (Rails, Svelte, …) override kit defaults.

Reference: `docs/stack-detection.md` in the kit tree (`kit_root` in `~/.cursor/kit-user-rules.manifest.json`).
